40,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,"I've found some revealing data. Last year, some of us barely saw each other all day, while in the shared house, there was no space for a moment of solitude. It seems our environment directly impacts our connection.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"That is a very important observation, Mizuki. I found that the inns offer a lovely way to stay together in one room, though the island houses might be a bit challenging with only one bathroom.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,1,talk,Minato,,"I found out that the inns have very strict times for meals, and we'd all sleep in one room on futons. The island houses only have one bathroom, and some people said the water gets cold. That sounds a bit scary.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"My research shows a significant difference in travel. The ferry schedule is quite restrictive, meaning two full days would be spent just on the journey. In contrast, the city options offer much more flexibility and less waiting.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,1,talk,Midori,,"I found that all-in rates can be a bit unfair to light eaters, as everyone pays the same regardless of appetite. Also, the offshore houses cost about 5,400 yen per person per night, but that doesn't include food.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Jonathan, spending two full days in transit seems excessive and could be draining. @Shizue, @Minato, the lack of bathrooms in houses and strict meal times at inns both present different kinds of stress for the group.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Jonathan"",""Shizue"",""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Mizuki, you are quite right. While sharing a room can be a wonderful way to bond, we must ensure that no one feels overwhelmed. A place where we can all rest peacefully is very important.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,2,talk,Minato,,"@Shizue, I agree. I'm a little worried about the cold water and the strict meal times. I wonder if there's a place where we can have a bit more freedom and a warm bath whenever we need it.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Minato, I agree that freedom and comfort are essential. When we consider the ferry's restrictive schedule, the journey itself becomes a chore. A destination with seamless transport would allow us to preserve our energy for the actual holiday.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@Jonathan, I agree that a seamless journey would be much more relaxing. I'm also a bit concerned about the offshore houses; since food is extra, the final cost could vary quite a bit from the initial estimate.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,3,talk,Mizuki,,It seems we are facing a trade-off between forced togetherness and total isolation. We need a destination that allows us to move as a group but provides enough space for individuals to breathe when needed.,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Midori, you make a very sensible point. If the costs are unpredictable, it might lead to some of us quietly bearing a heavier burden. I believe a clear, all-inclusive arrangement would be much kinder to everyone's peace of mind.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,3,talk,Minato,,I think it would be nice if we had a place where we don't have to worry about the water getting cold or being told exactly when to eat. Maybe a place with more rooms?,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"@Minato, I agree. A place with more rooms would provide the quietude we all need. If we combine that with a location that doesn't require days of travel, we can truly relax instead of recovering from the trip itself.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,3,talk,Midori,,"@Shizue, thank you for understanding. I agree that predictability is key. If we can find a way to know the total cost upfront, it would prevent any stress about the bill later on.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,2,4,talk,Mizuki,,"To summarize, we need a location that balances accessibility, financial predictability, and a layout that avoids both overcrowding and isolation. It sounds like we should prioritize a place that offers individual space without sacrificing our time together.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,2,4,talk,Shizue,,"I agree completely, Mizuki. Let us look for a place that is gentle on our spirits and our wallets. A destination that is easy to reach and clear in its costs will allow us to focus on our friendship.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,2,4,talk,Minato,,I agree! I hope we can find a place that's cozy and where we can all feel relaxed. I'm looking forward to seeing the options so we can pick the best one together!,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,I agree. A destination that minimizes the burden of travel and provides a serene environment will be the most rewarding. I look forward to seeing which options align with these needs.,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,2,4,talk,Midori,,I agree with everyone. Let's hope the options give us a clear total cost and a comfortable environment. I'm looking forward to seeing what we can choose together!,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
