65,3,1,talk,Mizuki,,"Looking at the options, Option A seems the most balanced. It provides a central hub for us to gather, but being in a town allows for that necessary individual space and flexibility that we found lacking in previous years.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"I agree, Mizuki. Option A sounds very lovely. The inn provides a warm place for us to gather, and since the meals are included, we can avoid any confusion or worry about the costs.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,1,talk,Minato,,"I like Option A too! It sounds cozy, and since it's in a town, maybe we can find a nice place to sit and relax. But I'm still a little worried about the meal times.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,"Option A is quite appealing. The train journey is efficient, avoiding the restrictive ferry schedules of Option B. It allows us to arrive and depart without losing entire days to the logistics of travel.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,1,talk,Midori,,I agree with everyone. Option A seems the most predictable financially since the meals are at the inn. It avoids the uncertainty of the island house costs and the fragmented billing of a city break.,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Minato, the meal times might be strict, but the freedom of the town during the day compensates for it. Option B is too crowded and Option C is too isolating, which we've already seen can be problematic.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Minato, dear, perhaps we can look at the meal times as a gentle way to ensure we all gather and share our day together. It creates a lovely rhythm for our trip, don't you think?","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,2,talk,Minato,,"@Shizue, I think that's a nice way to think about it. I just hope it's not too strict. But Option B sounds a bit scary with the cold water and only one bathroom for everyone.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Minato, I agree. The logistical constraints of Option B, combined with the shared facilities, would likely be quite draining. Option A offers a much more serene experience and a far more efficient journey.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,2,talk,Midori,,"@Minato, I agree. Option B's shared house sounds stressful, and the costs would be so unpredictable. Option A gives us a clear price and a comfortable stay, which makes it the most relaxing choice for everyone.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,3,talk,Mizuki,,"It seems we have a strong consensus. Option A avoids the extremes of the other two; it prevents the isolation of Option C and the overcrowding of Option B, ensuring we stay connected without feeling trapped. I vote for Option A.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,3,talk,Shizue,,"I agree completely. Option A is the most considerate choice, as it ensures we are all taken care of without any hidden costs or burdens. It will be a wonderful way to bond. I vote for Option A.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,3,talk,Minato,,"I'm a bit nervous about the meal times, but everyone else likes Option A, and it sounds much better than the cold water in Option B. I want us all to be happy! I vote for Option A.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,"I agree. Option A is the most peaceful choice, as it minimizes the time spent in transit and avoids the stress of restrictive schedules. It allows for a truly restful experience. I vote for Option A.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,3,talk,Midori,,I agree with everyone. Option A is the most responsible choice because it provides the financial clarity I value and the comfort we all need. It's the best way to ensure a harmonious trip. I vote for Option A.,"{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
80,3,4,talk,Mizuki,,It is a relief that we have reached such a clear and unanimous agreement. Option A provides the stability and balance we need to truly enjoy each other's company. I am happy to cast my final vote for Option A.,"{""words"":40,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
81,3,4,talk,Shizue,,It brings me such joy to see us all in harmony. Option A is a gentle choice that protects both our friendships and our peace of mind. I happily cast my final vote for Option A.,"{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
82,3,4,talk,Minato,,"I'm so glad we all agree! Even if I'm a little nervous, I know it'll be fun because we're all going together. I'll do my best to enjoy the meal times! I vote for Option A!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
83,3,4,talk,Jonathan,,I am pleased that we have found a solution that respects both our time and our need for tranquility. Option A is the most rational and serene choice. I vote for Option A.,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
84,3,4,talk,Midori,,I'm so happy we've found a destination that makes everyone feel comfortable and secure. Knowing the costs are clear and the journey is easy lets me truly relax. I vote for Option A!,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
